{"履修期": "秋学期", "主な教授言語": "英語", "授業目的": "本講義では学生が英語でコミュニケーションを取るための基本的な日常会話の語彙・文 法を修得することと、話す技術の向上を目的としている。", "到達目標": "See below", "特記事項": "", "関連科目": "", "授業の概要・背景": "Although there are regular homework assignments (20%), a strong emphasis is put on in-class participation and communication which is reflected in the Grading percentages (30%). Students who are considering taking this course should also note that there are no Mid-term or Final Assessment examinations, but there are two Poster Presentations (20%).", "授業方法": "Lecture:&nbsp;Faculty members explain the details of knowledge. Basically, the main learning activity for students is to take notes of the explanations made by faculty members. However, these are followed by question-and-answer sessions between faculty members and students.Group Work:&nbsp;Students make groups of four members or more to perform learning activities such as discussion, language analysis, negotiation, and translation.Presentation: Students summarize the results of their own learning activities and plan a short presentation to give to a partner. Additionally, students&nbsp;present a handmade A3 poster to a variety of rotating partners&nbsp;in the Reflection Poster Presentations - Sessions 6 &amp; 12.Assignment for next Session preparation - Homework: Students&nbsp;prepare for the next class by writing a Reflection Diary which will help them to create content for their Reflection Poster Presentation. Other weeks will require making vocabulary quizzes or transcribing recorded conversations.Flex Hours: A pre-course syllabus quiz will help students to understand course goals and activities. Midway through the course, students make new groups to collaborate on an audio podcast creation project which will be played to the class in Session 12.", "トピック": {"第1回": ["<div style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><span style=\"font-size:13.28px;\"><p style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-width:normal;font-size:13.3px;line-height:normal;font-f